# TwinCAT3 TcPlcObject XML Format

Applies to `.TcPOU`, `.TcDUT`, `.TcGVL`, and `.TcIO`. All share root `<TcPlcObject>` with ST (or empty) content inside `<![CDATA[...]]>`.

## Universal edit rules (all types)

1. **Only change CDATA / ST content** — `.TcPOU` / `.TcDUT` / `.TcGVL` / `.TcIO` are XML. Outside `<![CDATA[...]]>` change nothing (tags, attributes, whitespace between elements, `Version` / `ProductVersion`) unless you are intentionally creating a new object or adding a new Method/Property/Action element.
2. **Never copy or reuse GUIDs** — `Id="{...}"` values must never be copied from another element or file. Generate fresh UUIDs for new elements only; leave existing Ids untouched when editing code.
3. **Do not rewrite line endings** — TwinCAT files in repos are typically LF. When batch-writing (Python/scripts), do not force `\r\n`. Preserving the file’s existing newlines avoids Git treating every line as changed (as with forced CRLF rewrites).
4. **Do not touch encoding / BOM** — Keep the file’s existing encoding (UTF-8, with or without BOM). Do not “re-save” with a different encoding or strip/add a BOM unless the file was already that way.
5. **`Name` attribute must match** the type/member name inside the corresponding Declaration CDATA (`FUNCTION_BLOCK` / `FUNCTION` / `PROGRAM` / `INTERFACE` / `TYPE` / GVL name / `METHOD` / `PROPERTY`).

### Safe write pattern (scripts)

```python
# Read bytes → decode with detected encoding → edit CDATA only → encode same way → write bytes
# Use newline="" / write bytes so Python does not translate \n ↔ \r\n
path.write_bytes(edited_text.encode(detected_encoding))  # or open(..., "wb")
```

Prefer targeted CDATA edits (search/replace inside CDATA) over full XML re-serialize.

