## GUID rules

Every XML element with an `Id` attribute requires a GUID. GUIDs are the primary identity mechanism for TwinCAT objects — they link POUs, methods, properties, and actions across the solution.

### Format

Standard UUID v4, lowercase hex with hyphens, wrapped in curly braces:

```
Id="{a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890}"
```

- 8-4-4-4-12 hex digits: `{xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx}`
- Lowercase letters: `{a1b2...}` not `{A1B2...}`
- Always include curly braces in the XML attribute value

### Generation

Generate a fresh random GUID for each **new** element:

- PowerShell: `[guid]::NewGuid().ToString('D')` then wrap in `{}`
- Python: `import uuid; f'{{{uuid.uuid4()}}}'`

### Uniqueness scope

Every GUID must be **unique across the entire PLC project** (all `.TcPOU`, `.TcIO`, `.TcDUT`, `.TcGVL` files combined). Two different elements must never share the same GUID, even across different files.

### GUID count per element

| Element | GUIDs needed | Id locations |
|---------|:------------:|--------------|
| POU (FB / Function / Program) | 1 | `<POU Id="...">` |
| Interface (`<Itf>`) | 1 | `<Itf Id="...">` |
| Method | 1 | `<Method Id="...">` |
| Action | 1 | `<Action Id="...">` |
| Property (read-write) | 3 | `<Property Id="...">` + `<Get Id="...">` + `<Set Id="...">` |
| Property (read-only, no Set) | 2 | `<Property Id="...">` + `<Get Id="...">` |
| DUT (Struct / Enum / Union) | 1 | `<DUT Id="...">` |
| GVL | 1 | `<GVL Id="...">` |

### GUID do / don't

- **Never reuse** a GUID from another element — always generate fresh
- **Never change** an existing GUID when editing code — GUIDs are stable identifiers
- **Never omit** the `Id` attribute — TwinCAT requires it on every POU/Itf/Method/Property/Action/DUT/GVL (and Get/Set) element
- **Never copy-paste** a file without replacing ALL GUIDs with fresh ones
- **Never invent** GUIDs by typing hex digits — always use `uuid.uuid4()` or equivalent

### Fake GUID detection

The `--ensure-object-guids` repair detects AI-generated fake GUIDs that parse as valid UUIDs but contain obvious non-random patterns. These are replaced automatically with real `uuid.uuid4()` values.

Detected patterns (any single match triggers replacement):

- **Repeated digits**: 5+ consecutive identical hex digits (`00000`, `55555`, `aaaaa`)
- **Sequential ascending**: 5+ consecutive ascending hex digits (`56789`, `9abcd`, `bcdef`)
- **Sequential descending**: 5+ consecutive descending hex digits (`fedcb`, `98765`)
- **Low entropy**: fewer than 6 distinct hex digits in the 32-char hex string
- **Counter suffix**: last segment (12 hex) is 75%+ one digit with small counter (`555555555001`)
- **Known AI prefixes**: first 8 hex digits match known patterns (`d4e5f6a7`, `a1b2c3d4`, `12345678`, etc.)
- **Segment sequences**: 2+ of the five hyphen-separated segments are ascending hex runs
- **Mirrored segments**: adjacent segments are reversed copies (`abcd-dcba`)

